    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nGlobal variable having annotation and also `cython.declare()` causes failure with `redeclared` error.\n\n### Code to reproduce the behaviour:\n\n```cython\n\nimport cython\nfrom typing import Tuple, Any\n\n_Empty_Tuple: Tuple[Any, ...] = cython.declare(tuple, ())\n```\n\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\nI suppose annotation should be ignored since it is ignored in following case:\n```python\nimport cython\nfrom typing import Tuple, Any\n\n_Empty_Tuple: Tuple[Any, ...]\n```\n\nBut it is up to discussion.\n\n### OS\n\n_No response_\n\n### Python version\n\n_No response_\n\n### Cython version\n\nmaster\n\n### Additional context\n\nThis code already exist here: https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/blob/d9b44cb731bd27e6e82c99a3c0fb598214e8e7ff/lib/sqlalchemy/engine/_util_cy.py#L45",
    "closed_at": "2026-08-01T20:28:51Z",
