    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Right, I think annotations should always go second. If there is an explicit Cython declaration, it should be ignored.\n\nIn this concrete case, it would seem helpful to consider it an addition to the existing declaration and the container type could be augmented.\n\nBut I still think that explicit Cython declarations should take precedence. This specific case might just be an outlier that is not worth changing the rules. There might be a (non-historical) reason why the explicit Cython type was chosen like this, and we shouldn't try to second-guesd our users' intent.\n\nAt most, a performance hint could be justified.\n",
            "created_at": "2026-07-31T06:24:27Z",
